# masc written/email/w3c/lists-046-11493928
Numbering in lists, or sub-numbering in equations, is interrupted.
Example: a numbered list with items 1, 2, 3, is followed by a paragraph of text (the || is on the same level as the |<l>|), and then the list continues 4, 5, 6.
The intention of the author appears to be {\em one\/} list, but this list is interrupted.
A similar example can be found in equation sub-numbering: equations (4a) and (4b) are followed by a paragraph of text, followed by equations (4c) and (4d).

